%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% View 3 — gate sequence. Coverage baseline precedes every production edit;
%% fault injection precedes trusting the tests.
%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Preflight
    Preflight --> CoverageTool: HEAD == origin/main
    CoverageTool --> Baseline: cargo-llvm-cov 0.9.0 installed
    CoverageTool --> Halt: not installable without repo change
    Baseline --> Restructure: baseline recorded BEFORE any production edit
    Restructure --> FaultInjection: 63 tests preserved, helpers deduplicated
    FaultInjection --> CommitVV: all 4 mutants killed, source restored by hash
    FaultInjection --> Strengthen: a mutant survives or is caught by only one test
    Strengthen --> FaultInjection
    CommitVV --> CoreMigration
    CoreMigration --> CoreGates
    CoreGates --> HnnMigration: coverage not down, equivalence proved
    CoreGates --> Halt: any new failure
    HnnMigration --> HnnGates
    HnnGates --> Publish
    HnnGates --> Halt: any new failure
    Publish --> [*]

    note right of Baseline
        Known 57/58 drift stays visible and failing
        in the normal gate. It is skipped ONLY during
        profile collection, by command line, never in
        source. A second skip is needed for a timed
        throughput assertion that instrumentation
        invalidates by construction.
    end note

    note right of FaultInjection
        Coverage says a line ran.
        It does not say a wrong result
        would have been noticed.
        The mutants are what establish that.
    end note
